  "concept": {
    "movement": "A deliberate four-beat armored amble with full short steps and a steady shell. Faster travel is a compact scurry driven by the legs beneath the shell, with little bounce or lateral roll.",
    "attack": "Brace the hind feet, lower the snout and rake forward and down with the left foreclaw, followed by the right. The armored torso stays supported while each strong claw makes a clear reaching stroke and returns to its planted track.",
    "death": "The snout lowers, the legs fold under the armored body and release into a supported flank. The shell retains its shape; head, rear body and narrow tail settle into a still grounded finish."
